# Test: a live edit of service { as112 } reaches the as112 plugin
# Initial config: as112 serves ipv4-only with hostname node-a.example.
# After SIGHUP:   address-family is ipv6-only and hostname is node-b.example.
# Expected: as112 installs the reloaded config at apply, logs it with the new
#           address family, and answers the HOSTNAME.AS112.NET TXT query with
#           the new hostname on the IPv6 loopback, which only the reloaded
#           config binds.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-plugin-reload-applies-or-refuses row 22, AC-1: as112's
#            verify/apply pair runs the configure path for the reloaded
#            config (as112Installer.install), and the DNS listener answers
#            from it.
# PREVENTS: the acked-and-dropped reload. With OnConfigure alone, the SDK
#           answers config-apply OK and calls nothing, so the commit succeeded
#           while as112 kept the boot config until a restart.
#
# DISCRIMINATION: client/dns-query asks tls://[::1]:$PORT for the TXT of
# hostname.as112.net. until it carries node-b.example (RFC 7534 Section 3.5,
# the node identification zone). Only the apply handler binds ::1 and
# publishes the reloaded hostname: with OnConfigure alone the client is
# refused, then fails, and the "ipv6-only" expectation fails too. That an edit elsewhere under service publishes nothing
# is proven in Go by TestConfigTxUnchangedSubtreeIsNoop
# (as112/config_tx_unchanged_test.go).

# The client asks over DNS over TLS on the leased port. as112 serves cleartext
# DNS on port 53 only (as112Port), which an unprivileged host cannot bind:
# Linux refuses every port below 1024 and Darwin refuses 127.0.0.1:53. The
# cleartext listeners fail and are logged, and the DoT listener on loopback
# answers from the same snapshot (answerQuery). With no cert-file, Ze serves
# an ephemeral self-signed certificate.

option=env:var=ze.log.as112:value=info

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
service {
	as112 {
		enabled true
		address-family ipv4-only
		hostname node-a.example
		tls {
			enabled true
			listen-port $PORT
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

tmpfs=config2.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF2
service {
	as112 {
		enabled true
		address-family ipv6-only
		hostname node-b.example
		tls {
			enabled true
			listen-port $PORT
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF2

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=le test fixture reload/tx-protocol-sighup-trigger
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=20s
await=stderr:contains=sighup reload complete
expect=stderr:pattern=as112: config applied.*address-family=ipv4-only
expect=stderr:pattern=as112: config applied.*address-family=ipv6-only
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=le test fixture client/dns-query tls://[::1]:$PORT hostname.as112.net. TXT node-b.example
expect=stderr:contains=OK: dns TXT hostname.as112.net. served node-b.example
reject=stderr:contains=reload error
reject=stderr:pattern=panic
